# =============================================================================
# pogo_extract/.gitignore      (2026-09-29: code + docs in git, data on the phone)
#
# WHITELIST style. Everything is ignored unless a rule in section 2-4 re-allows it.
# Git rules: the LAST matching rule wins, and a file inside an ignored DIRECTORY can
# never be re-allowed -- so section 5 (deny) and section 6 (directories) must stay LAST.
#
# Why whitelist: this folder is ~3.0 GB of which ~99% is personal game data, memory
# dumps, phone binaries, caches and backups. New junk (a *.log, a new *.db.bak,
# a dumped .bin) must not sneak into the repo, and a new secret must not be pushed by
# accident. A file that the cloud needs but is missing fails LOUDLY; a leaked token does not.
# To publish a new reference file: add an anchored "!/name" line in section 4.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. DEFAULT DENY ---------------------------------------------------------
*
# re-open every directory so the allow rules below can reach files inside them
!*/

# --- 2. ALLOW: CODE ----------------------------------------------------------
# The cull pipeline (full_audit.py, pogo_pipeline.py, keep_config.py, dashboard.py,
# system/scripts/*.py), the audits, the one-off analysis scripts, the Frida/IL2CPP
# JS agents (bulk_tag.js, full_inventory.js, ...), phone helper shells.
# Backups such as x.py.bak-2026*, x.py.ultrabak, x.py.kalibak, x.py.orig never match
# these (their names do not END in .py) and stay ignored.
!.gitignore
!*.py
!*.js
!*.sh
!*.vbs

# --- 3. ALLOW: DOCS ----------------------------------------------------------
# LAW.md, RUNBOOK.md, HANDOFF_KEEP_LAW.md, RESUME.md, SELF_UPDATE.md, .grill/*.md,
# system/*.md, system/procedures/*.md, research_2026-05-27/*.md, ...
!*.md
!CLAUDE.md
# the two hand-written HTML docs (everything else .html is generated by gen_*.py)
!/RCA_POGO_CRASHES.html
!/POKEMOD_IMPLEMENTATION_MAP.html

# --- 4. ALLOW: STATIC REFERENCE DATA + HAND-EDITED CONFIG ---------------------
# Only files that change by a CODE CHANGE (reviewed, committed). Everything the pipeline itself rewrites -- pokemon.db,
# keep_config.json (per account: switch_account.py swaps it), the walk outputs, the monthly game-master refresh
# (pvpoke_gamemaster.json, gamemaster_pokeminers.json, pvpoke_rankings/), the live registries -- is DATA and lives on the
# phone (tools/pogo_data.py, tools/data_manifest.txt [inventory]). One copy each: git never holds a file the data store holds.
!/curation_config.json
!/curation_labels.json
!/gender_variants.json
!/system/tags/registry.json
!/form_enum.json
!/form_category.json
!/form_to_dex.json
!/costume_enum.json
!/location_card_enum.json
!/move_id_to_name.json
!/proto_layout.json
# the master-plan workflow output gen_master_plan.py renders (static)
!/wf_master.json
# Bag Pulse pictures + the game's own names (bag_art.py --refresh-index / --refresh-names writes them, pogo_display.py reads them):
# a fresh clone and CI need both, and the default deny above would hide them
!/pogo_icon_index.txt
!/official_names_en.json

# --- 5. DENY: things the allow rules above would otherwise let in ------------
# 5a. SECRETS / AUTH / SESSION (defense in depth; the default deny already blocks them)
Hawk2.xml
nia_secret_*
*secret*
*token*
*cookie*
*credential*
*passw*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
*.sqlite
.env
.env.*
playerprefs.xml
pokemod_prefs.xml
gameData.xml
# 5b. generated / stale personal reports and docs that name his mons or his e-mail
ACCOUNT_REPORT.md
collection_summary.md
cull_summary.md
CULL_EXPLAINED.md
dex_completion_advice.md
review_candidates_summary.md
verification_sample.md
data_quality.md
phone_storage_survey.md
niantic_api_replay_v2.md
niantic_api_replay_research.md
/system/analysis/MASTER_COLLECTION.md
# 5c. one-off Claude-Code workflow scripts (results live elsewhere)
/.wf_*.js
# 5d. backups (defense in depth): *.bak*, *.orig, *.pre_*, *.pre0*, *bak, *.d5bak ...
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak_*
*.bak.*
*.orig
*.pre_*
*.pre0*
*.kalibak
*.ultrabak
*.studiobak
*.uxbak
*.d5bak
*.f467bak
*.cap2bak
*.batterybak
*.downloaded
# 5e. caches / compiled / generated binaries
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pkl
*.tmp
# 5f. personal game databases, snapshots, SQLite side files
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.*
*.gz
*.xz
# 5g. logs, pid files
*.log
*.pid
# 5h. big binaries (phone-side tools, dumps, APK/JAR/dex, Frida/Pokemod payloads)
*.so
*.pyd
*.bin
*.dat
*.dex
*.apk
*.jar
*.arsc
/frida-server
/frida-inject
/pokemod-injector-arm64
/injector
/main_agent
/vpgp_agent

# 5i. scripts that break the hard rules (release, tag nukes outside safe_nuke_tags.py, force-stopping PoGo, unattended
#     daemons). They stay on the PC for the record; the repo the cloud runs from -- with the phone reachable -- never
#     carries them (repo-prep critic, 2026-09-29).
/bulk_release.py
/_nuke_all_tags.py
/_nuke_tags.py
/system/scripts/nuke_all_tags.py
/fix_remote_trade_binding.py
/fix_remote_trade_dupe.py
/autocull_watch.py
/start_autocull.vbs
/run_bulk_tag.py
/self_update.py
/SELF_UPDATE.md
/_commons_trim_more.py
/orchestrate.py
/run_rename.py
/spawn_inject.py
/diag_hook.py
# 5j. stale policy docs (old caps -- dangerous to act on) and third-party RE research the tooling does not use
/system/KEEP_POLICY.md
/system/analysis/KEEP_POLICY_DRYRUN.md
/existing_tools_survey.md
/ipogo_features.md
/ipogo_features_v2.md
/ipogo_filter_schema.md
/libnotmain_decrypt_research.md
/dump_libnotmain.sh
/mem_write_codeexec_research.md
/niantic_replay.py
/pokemod_extraction_attempt.md
/zygote_injection_research.md

